favor other accounts over the Partnership; (viii) the General Partner has an 
incentive to discourage redemptions because the IB Affiliated with the 
General Partner receives a portion of the fixed commissions based on the Net 
Asset Value of the Partnership assigned to be traded; (ix) the General 
Partner, the CTAs and their principals and affiliates may trade in the 
commodity markets for their own accounts and may take positions opposite or 
ahead of those taken for the Partnership; and, (x) the CTAs are compensated 
based on a percentage of the New Net Profit of the Partnership and thus may 
have an incentive to engage in ill-advised trades.  See "Conflicts of 
