may be the result of factors like the suspension of trading because of "daily 
price limits".  Most United States commodity exchanges limit movement in a 
single direction in one trading day by rules referred to as "daily price 
limits".  These limits provide that no trades may be executed at prices 
beyond the daily limits.  Once the price of a futures contract for a 
particular commodity has increased or decreased by an amount equal to the 
